{"id":"9b33870f-b443-42ca-90c8-63e7edf9caa0","title":"Week 10: Lambda calculus","description":"Recall that, in the Proto language, numerals are evaluated in the same way as Church numerals. So, for example, ((3 f) x) reduces to (f (f (f x))). As a shorthand, I will often write (f³ x) in place of (f (f (f x))).
Recall that the following reductions are allowed:
- α-renaming, i.e. λx.E[x] ↝ λy.E[y], where y is a new variable;
- β-reduction, i.e. (λx.E[x] A) ↝ E[A]; and
- η-reduction, i.e. λx.(E x) ↝ E, where E does not contain x as a free variable.","courseId":"59267dce-f1f8-482e-b038-f8c97bb43981","courseName":"41080 Theory of Computing Science - Spring 2026","dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:59:59Z"}

